WEBVTT

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.000
What's wrong?

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.320
Surprised that the gun you thought you'd 
swapped out is firing live bullets?

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:37.120
You wanted to get the drop on me 
as payback for roping you into this...

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.720
And it's that attitude of yours 
that screws things up for you.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:46.010
I didn't aim for your heart 
for a reason. Wanna know why?

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.730
Because I wanted you to witness 
my moment of victory.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:41.070
Sorry, but I tossed the little toy you 
rigged my car with into the river.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.850
Damn it! I'll kill him—

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:15.970
Don't bother, Chlo.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.290
We got what we came for.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.010
<b>The Man Who Abandoned "Lupin"</b>

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.540
He really got one over on you!

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.960
I can't believe that punk Albert would 
go as far as stealing the cash first,

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.050
just because he knew I was coming for it.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.340
Not to mention, replacing the 
whole stash with counterfeit bills...

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.550
Pretty slick.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:34.560
Dammit!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.890
He even had the nerve to leave real bills 
bookending each pile just to sell the trick.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:40.170
Are you sure about that?

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.810
Looks like Albert's upped his game again.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.080
Dammit!

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.590
I'm glad you're awake,

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.810
but with your injuries, you'd be better off 
coming to without screaming.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.620
How long was I out?

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:27.610
Two, maybe three days.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.110
I'm sorry, man.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:33.820
Cut that out.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:38.140
Just the thought of you getting all 
grateful is making me break out in hives.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.340
I see that you have awakened.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.240
Yeah.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:49.730
Sorry about all this.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.760
Seems I caused a bit of trouble.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:56.010
Please stop. An apology from you 
is enough to give me a nervous rash.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.850
I assume this means we will be splitting 
tonight's dinner three ways.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.390
Oh, is that an eel?

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.950
Looks like we're in for quite a treat.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:11.710
Actually, this is a treat 
even finer than eel.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.360
<i>And now, we turn to the heated 
presidential election...</i>

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.490
<i>Former prime minister, 
Mr. Arbeau, and Mr. Beckel,</i>

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.620
<i>who has been picking up support 
from the moderate left,</i>

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.140
<i>have emerged as the front-runners.</i>

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:33.280
<i>Trailing in their wake is "The Eye of the Storm,"
 AKA right-wing candidate, Mr. Calvess,</i>

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:37.650
<i>who's come in for increasing criticism 
over his staunch anti-immigrant rhetoric,</i>

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.890
<i>and he's seen support for 
his campaign stagnate.</i>

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:44.640
<i>That being said, he's made it this far 
on an anti-immigrant platform,</i>

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:47.970
<i>so only time will tell if his support base...</i>

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:54.650
Revenant?

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.660
You're alive?

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.910
We all thought you'd bought it, 
since you never checked in.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.910
I'd love to embrace you and 
welcome you back into the fold,

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:08.660
but I told you to steal this thing,

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:10.920
and kill Lupin and Camille 
while you were at it.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:13.230
You screwed up.

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:16.710
Now, I'm a merciful leader...

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.170
...but there has to be
a price to pay for failure.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:50.580
Chow down like that and you'll have 
crumbs pouring out of your wounds.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:54.600
It looks as if you might be able 
to sleep easier tonight.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:57.460
I sure hope so.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:01.970
This "Albert" person must really 
be getting under your skin.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:07.860
Hey, now, Goemon...

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:11.110
You were calling his name 
as you tossed and turned.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.290
He's the man who abandoned "Lupin."

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.530
Albert.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.510
You leaving?

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.000
Yeah.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.000
I'll be taking the title of "the Third," then.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.370
Suit yourself.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:45.010
You're seriously accepting 
defeat so gracefully?

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.010
Of course not.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:50.020
You should know that better than anyone.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.260
Then, what's the big idea?!

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:55.270
I'm sick of these small-time jobs.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:59.280
I'm gonna aim at something bigger.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:03.270
"Bigger"? Gonna steal the moon or something?

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.400
No. France.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.520
Has Guillaume made a move?

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.570
None that arouses suspicion 
for the time being.

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:26.300
Though, it's hard to tell, since his "normal" 
activities are already suspicious...

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.690
And what about José?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.530
We've got people on the 
lookout all over town,

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.810
but we've been unable to 
locate him or his people.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.060
What are you talking about, José?

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.830
Are you deaf?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.790
I'm not going to give you the notebook.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:50.690
I've found a much better use for it 
than whatever you had planned.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:04.350
We've been unable to confirm, but 
the current casualty count stands at 22.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:08.610
The Cry for Truth terrorist group claimed 
responsibility shortly before it happened.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:14.100
The Cry for Truth? Wasn't the 
DGSE monitoring them?

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.070
Yes, sir.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.870
They should've had a pretty full picture of 
everything the terrorists were planning...

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:20.640
Then, why?

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:23.790
<i>He let it happen.</i>

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.610
<i>But why?</i>

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:29.080
We let notorious terrorists 
into the country,

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.620
and now, we're supposed to 
turn a blind eye to them!

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:35.460
Interior Minister, if we 
don't follow his demands...

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.370
I know!

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:40.370
He's got the black notebook, 
a veritable Pandora's Box.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:44.890
But if <i>this </i>one is opened, 
even hope will make itself scarce!

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.540
Things are getting kinda hairy, huh?

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:07.540
It seems as though the "hairiness" 
has found its way here.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:32.800
Y'know, it opens from the inside...

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.880
He didn't have to smash through it.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:38.310
Must just be Goemon's style.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:53.610
I really liked that room. 
It had great natural lighting.

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.180
It wasn't exactly well-ventilated, though.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.760
I know just how to fix that.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.150
Okay...

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:02.630
Catch!

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.270
You ready to do this?

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.770
Lupin, carry on without me.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:32.530
I guess that means the bastard survived...

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:53.500
We're jumping it!

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.100
Right!

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:08.480
Too bad!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.400
Lupin! Over here!

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:01.280
Chew on this!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.040
What?!

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.860
The foes who have targeted us 
are highly dangerous.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:34.300
And we don't even have the 
damn notebook anymore.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.160
The fewer people who know 
its secrets, the better.

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:43.660
Especially if they're planning on using said 
secrets for the purposes of skulduggery.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:50.550
Then, they will pursue us unremittingly, 
since we know the contents of the notebook.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.170
Hit the nail on the head.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:55.180
Then, we've only got one option.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:58.990
Yep. "The best defense is a good offense."

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:01.170
I think Buddha said that.

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:04.190
Wasn't it Confucius?

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.190
It was Sun Tzu.

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:16.210
Well... I'm not sure, actually.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:19.930
France is in the midst of a crisis!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:25.720
And these animals we call terrorists must 
be repelled by a strong, firm hand!

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:31.750
I have faith that you all... 
will empower me to do just that!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:35.290
Calvess! Calvess! Calvess!

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:39.680
Support for Candidate Calvess has 
skyrocketed almost overnight.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:45.450
In the past, his right-leaning tendencies 
have been viewed as something of a handicap,

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:50.810
but the recent spate of terrorist attacks 
has changed the public's outlook.

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:56.320
Do you think it's likely that Calvess 
will win the presidential election?

00:16:56.320 --> 00:17:01.690
If the terrorist attacks continue 
at this pace, he stands a good chance.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:06.840
I get it. So that's what he's after...

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.590
So far, so good, wouldn't you say?

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:14.260
Just one last push is needed, I reckon.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:20.100
A final fireworks display before the day 
of the election, and we'll be set.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:24.010
Yeah. And then, France will be ours.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.100
What are we going to do?

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:31.160
Criticism of the police is 
growing with every passing day.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:33.780
If we don't do something soon,
 it's going to get to the point where—

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.860
Then, what do you suggest we do?!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:48.230
<i>No one wants to make a move with 
the black notebook still in play, huh?</i>

00:17:55.580 --> 00:18:01.480
Who would've guessed a civil war would break out 
as soon as we touched down here on a job?

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.500
Our luck sucks, doesn't it?

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:10.950
What now? At this rate, the city and the 
palace are gonna be swarming with troops.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.400
Still gotta go for it, right?

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.660
If we don't, we can kiss Africa's biggest 
diamond, Gaia's Navel, goodbye.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:18.970
The army will get their paws on it.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:23.120
Are you serious? It's practically suicide!

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:26.100
Suits me. More thrills 
and spills this way, right?

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:31.720
Besides, someone's set their sights 
on the loot we're gunning for.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.220
If you're ready to sit back 
and let them take it...

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.880
...I'm not sure you're 
cut out to be a thief.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.500
<i>France is mine.</i>

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.570
<i>I'm not letting them take it.</i>

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:49.700
What's got you in such a rush?

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:53.480
Lupin!

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:56.660
I'm guessing the idea of someone 
else stealing your score

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:59.540
got you so anxious that you just 
<i>had</i> to do something, right?

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:03.340
Maybe you're still a thief, after all.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:05.570
Didn't I explain it to you already?

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:10.340
I only became a cop so I could 
go after a much bigger target.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:12.350
And what brings you here?

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.850
Who, me? Just thought I'd ask 
our mutual friend here

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:19.110
about the pests that have been 
swarming around me lately.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.730
Then, our interests align nicely.

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:28.610
I'll leave the interrogation to you.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:36.650
You've got a knack for getting bad 
guys to spill their guts, right?

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:40.920
Albert! What do you think you're doing?!

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.560
Do you honestly think you'll get away with—

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:49.720
I'm the one asking the questions here!

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:19.920
I gotta say, the guys that are after us
 this time are pretty hardcore.

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:23.790
Close combat, firearms... They're using the 
whole kit and caboodle to try to snuff us out.

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:27.250
I guess anyone who'd want to pull off a coup 
in France must be made of sterner stuff.

00:22:27.250 --> 00:22:31.550
Making enemies out of us 
was a mistake, though.

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:38.050
Come on, Albert, let's show 
these jerks how thieves fight.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:45.040
<b>Thief and Thief</b>

00:22:38.050 --> 00:22:40.010
Next time: Thief and Thief

00:22:40.010 --> 00:22:41.960
You may have abandoned "Lupin,"

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:44.280
but you get a front-row seat 
to see what he's really capable of.
